--TEST--
A constructor does not write a `readonly` property inside a loop, because the loop can run the write twice (`rule:classes/lateinit-restrictions`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The loop body can run more than once, so the write inside it can be a
// second write. Computing the value in a local variable is the fix.
class Total {
    public readonly ?int $last;

    public function constructor(array<int> $items) {
        foreach ($items as int $item) {
            $this->last = $item;
        }
    }
}

class Fixed {
    public readonly int $sum;

    public function constructor(array<int> $items) {
        int $sum = 0;
        foreach ($items as int $item) {
            $sum += $item;
        }
        $this->sum = $sum;
    }
}

var $t = new Fixed([1, 2]);
// covers: lang:classes/properties
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0782]: `Total::$last` is `readonly`, so the constructor writes it only once
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
